{
 "title": "Choosing the Weights of Small Open Language Models: code, per-item evaluation caches and ten preprints",
 "upload_type": "software",
 "version": "1.0.0",
 "language": "eng",
 "access_right": "open",
 "license": "MIT",
 "description": "<p>Code, per-item evaluation caches and analysis scripts that regenerate every number, table and figure of ten preprints on choosing and combining the weights of small open language models (Qwen2.5-0.5B, SmolLM2-360M, Pythia-160M): linear and spherical interpolation, task-vector extrapolation, three-model merges (TIES, DARE), layer-group search, checkpoint averaging, the winner's curse in validation-based selection, validation-set size and the language-modeling cost of interpolation. Each evaluation is stored as a 0/1 vector per item, so the statistics can be reproduced without a GPU. Most results are null or negative and are reported as such. The ten papers are CC BY 4.0 (Figshare); the code is MIT.</p>",
 "creators": [
